# Paths that ripgrep and other tools that read .ignore files leave out of searches by default. Run rg -uu to search
# them anyway.

# Recorded agent sessions that each release's changelog cites as evidence. Their JSON event logs hold lines hundreds of
# kilobytes long, so a search that matches them fills the searching agent's context with machine-written text instead
# of source. The pattern has no leading folder because ripgrep applies a parent folder's anchored pattern only to
# searches that start in that folder.
captures/
